@@ -70,6 +70,16 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to :meth:`~rich.console.Console.print` and :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log`. It converts each object to a string with its normal string conversion, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``. Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("foo", "bar", sep=", ", style="bold")
+
+``out`` does not pretty print containers, word wrap or crop the output, process console markup, or replace emoji codes. Text is written literally. It does apply highlighting, which is on by default; pass ``highlight=False`` to turn it off, or ``highlight=None`` to use the console's setting. It also accepts a basic ``style``, which is applied the same way as with ``print``.
+
+
